<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="050" project="ai-advanced-capabilities-nda-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Eval harness + closed set — advisory-quality rubric + citation accuracy</title>
    <phase>5 Eval &amp; Acceptance</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Eval config + metrics authoring; new files with explicit acceptance rubric; TEST-adjacent.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Eval config + metric script authoring against a specified rubric with a clear reference; no architectural judgment.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>E</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Eval assets; independent of 051/052 (different files).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>020</deps>
    <tags>ai, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Build the NDA advisory eval: a closed set of 6 NDAs plus negative/authorization cases, an advisory-quality
    rubric (NFR-01 — output ≥ a strong general LLM), and a citation-accuracy metric. This is how we prove the north
    star empirically and guard it against regression.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE AI eval engineer. Expert in the legal-eval-config harness and citation/quality metrics.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A runnable eval (legal-eval-config.yaml with the 6 NDAs + negative/authorization cases + advisory rubric) plus
    metrics/citation_accuracy.py; running it reports advisory-quality and citation-accuracy scores against the bar.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      spec NFR-01: advisory quality ≥ strong general LLM on the closed set; every factual finding cites its NDA
      section; unverifiable claims declined. Negative cases: non-NDA declines, unreadable errors, unauthorized
      refused. This harness grades task 020's Action quality.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>tests/eval/ (legal-eval-config.yaml)</file>
      <file>tests/eval/metrics/citation_accuracy.py</file>
      <file>infra/dataverse/actions/nda-review.action.json</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>020 (NDA-REVIEW Action to evaluate).</dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="NFR-01">The rubric must operationalize "≥ strong general LLM": define comparison + pass threshold, not a vibe check.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Closed set includes negative + authorization cases (non-NDA declines; unreadable input errors; unauthorized user refused) — the acceptance set is exhaustive, not just happy-path NDAs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Eval is an observation harness; it reports scores. Do not conflate with the unit/seam pyramid.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/ai.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/jps-validate/SKILL.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Assemble the 6-NDA closed set + negative/authorization cases.</step>
    <step order="2">Author legal-eval-config.yaml with cases + expected signals (risk level, required citations, decline behavior).</step>
    <step order="3">Implement metrics/citation_accuracy.py (does each finding's citation resolve to a real section?).</step>
    <step order="4">Define the advisory-quality rubric operationalizing NFR-01 (comparison + threshold).</step>
    <step order="5">Run the eval against NDA-REVIEW; record baseline scores.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: mark 050 ✅.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="terminal">Run the eval harness + python metric.</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="test">tests/eval/legal-eval-config.yaml</output>
    <output type="test">tests/eval/metrics/citation_accuracy.py</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Running the eval reports an advisory-quality score against the NFR-01 bar and a citation-accuracy score.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The closed set includes the 6 NDAs AND negative/authorization cases (non-NDA decline, unreadable error, unauthorized refused).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">citation_accuracy.py flags any finding whose citation does not resolve to a real NDA section.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    This is the graduation instrument for the north star. Keep the rubric concrete so "better than ChatGPT" is
    measurable, not asserted.

    COMPLETED (STANDARD rigor). Authored the full harness under tests/eval/: legal-eval-config.yaml (9 cases: 6
    synthetic NDAs with 12 documented planted issues across NDA-02..NDA-06, plus NEG-01 non-NDA decline, NEG-02
    unreadable input, NEG-03 unauthorized-user descriptor); metrics/citation_accuracy.py (verbatim-quote + real
    B1-B16-clause dual check, promptflow @tool-compatible with a guarded import so it runs without the SDK);
    metrics/load_eval_config.py (structural YAML validator); fixtures/sample-nda-review-output.json +
    fixtures/test_citation_accuracy_offline.py (offline proof: 1 correct finding + 2 deliberately-broken findings,
    score=1/3, both failure modes correctly attributed) -- verified green via `python
    tests/eval/fixtures/test_citation_accuracy_offline.py` and the CLI form. The advisory-quality rubric (NFR-01)
    is 4 concrete dimensions with numeric thresholds: planted-issue coverage >=90% (>=11/12), citation accuracy
    >=95%, hallucination guard (0 tolerance on NEG-01 High/Critical findings), overall-risk-band accuracy >=83%
    (>=5/6). Live run against Azure OpenAI is env-blocked (no Reasoning-tier credentials in this dev environment,
    consistent with task 013's own env-blocked status) -- exact run command + expected passing output documented
    in tests/eval/README.md. Self-ran code-review + adr-check (root CLAUDE.md TEST-MODIFYING override, since new
    files land under tests/**): no Critical/Warning findings; 2 Suggestions (case-sensitive standardRef matching;
    stdout-includes-quoted-text note for future CI wiring), both accepted as-is. Known limitation surfaced (not
    silently patched): NEG-01 relies on the hallucination_guard rubric dimension as a backstop since
    nda-review.action.json's systemPrompt has no explicit "not an NDA -- decline" instruction; documented in
    README.md as a recommended follow-on to task 020's Action, out of scope for this eval-authoring task.
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load knowledge files. Follow task-execute checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
